          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em simplicial ring
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+object"} simplicial object
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ring"} Ring
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rings"} rings
          %p This may be understood conceptually as follows:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                as ordinary rings are algebras over the ordinary
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+theory"} algebraic theory
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                of rings, if we regard this as an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-algebraic+theory"} (∞,1)-algebraic theory
                then simplicial rings model the
                = succeed "-algebras" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %li
              %p
                the category
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ring"} Ring
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mrow
                        %mi op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {}^{op}
                is naturally equipped with the structure of a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+%28for+structured+%28infinity%2C1%29-toposes%29"} pregeometry
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+%28for+structured+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-toposes%29"} geometry (for structured (∞,1)-toposes)
                is
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi sRing
                          %mi op
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sRing^{op}
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            A
            %strong simplicial ring
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+object"} simplicial object
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ring"} Ring
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rings"} rings
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#connected_components Connected components
          %p
            Given a simplicial ring
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A = A_{\bullet}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+components"} connected components
            (the 0th “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+group"}> homotopy group
            ”)) is an ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Ring
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\pi_0(A) \in Ring
                  \\,.
          %p
            Forming connected components is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            from simplicial rings to plain rings, which is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            to the inclusion of ordinary rings as simplicially constant simplicial rings, exhibiting a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategory"} reflective subcategory
            inclusion
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ring
                  %mover
                    %mo ↪
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟵
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi π
                          %mn 0
                  %msup
                    %mi Ring
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi op
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Ring \stackrel{\stackrel{\pi_0}{\longleftarrow}}{\hookrightarrow} Ring^{\Delta^{op}}
                  \\,.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "Toen14"}> Toën 14, section 2.2
            )
          %p
            So on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+duals"} formal duals
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative
            (simplicial) rings this is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coreflection"} coreflection
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+schemes"} affine schemes
            in affine
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+schemes"} derived schemes
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi CRing
                    %mi op
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟵
                    %mo ↪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi CRing
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi op
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi op
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  CRing^{op}
                  \\stackrel{\hookrightarrow}{\longleftarrow}
                  (CRing^{\Delta^{op}})^{op}
                  \\,.
          %p
            Notice that coreflective embeddings are also given for instance by the inclusion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifolds"} manifolds
            into
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+manifolds"} formal manifolds
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+neighbourhoods"} infinitesimal neighbourhoods
            of formal duals of plain rings.
          %h3#higher_homotopy_groups Higher homotopy groups
          %p
            The higher
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_n(A)
            of a simplicial ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_\bullet
            are naturally
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules"} modules
            over the ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0(A)
            of connected components, so
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_\bullet
            is weakly
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contractible"} contractible
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0(A)=0
          %p (Again this is a manifestation of the simplicial ring being just an infinitesimal thickening of its connected components.)
          %p
            Notice that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0(A)
            is equivalently the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cokernel"} cokernel
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mn 0
                    %mo −
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_0-d_1 \colon A_1 \longrightarrow A_0
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/face+maps"} face maps
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi n
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_n \longrightarrow A_0
            compose with the projection to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0(A)
            is independent of the choices. These maps
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi n
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  A_n \longrightarrow \pi_0(A)
          %p
            give a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surjective"} surjective
            map from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_\bullet
            to the constant simplicial ring
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0(A)
          %p
            (This is just the simplest piece of the
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Postnikov+tower"} Postnikov tower
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≠
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0(A)\neq 0
            we can then compose with a surjective map to a constant simplicial field.
          %h3#model_category_structure Model category structure
          %p
            There is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            structure on simplicial rings that presents
            = succeed "-rings." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+T-algebras"} model structure on simplicial T-algebras
            for more.
          %p
            We describe here the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            presentation of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            of modules over simplicial rings.
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            be a simplicial commutative algebra. Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mi SMod
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A SMod
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            which, with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            regarded as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
            in the category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SAb
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SAb
            of abelian
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+group"} simplicial group
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SAb
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SAb
          %ul
            %li
              objects are abelian
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+group"} simplicial group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
              equipped with an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi N
                    %mo →
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \otimes N \to N
              of simplicial abelian groups;
          %p
            Equip
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mi SMod
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A SMod
            with the structure of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            by setting:
          %ul
            %li
              a morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_1\to N_2
              of
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules"} modules
              is a weak equivalence resp. a fibration precisely if the underlying morphism of
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} model structure on simplicial sets
          %p
            %strong Proposition
            This defines a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            structure which is
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrantly+generated+model+category"}> cofibrantly generated
                ;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+model+category"}> proper
                ;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cellular+model+category"}> cellular
                \.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#simplicial_fields Simplicial fields
          %p
            All simplicial
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fields"} fields
            are simplicially constant. This is because the composite
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mn 0
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi s
                        %mn 0
                        %mi n
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi n
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi d
                        %mn 0
                        %mi n
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_0\xrightarrow{s_0^n}A_n\xrightarrow{d_0^n}A_0
            is the identity, so
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi d
                    %mn 0
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_0^n
            is surjective, but all field homomorphisms are injective, so
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi d
                    %mn 0
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_0^n
            is an isomorphism.
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+algebra"} simplicial algebra
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+T-algebras"} model structure on simplicial T-algebras
          %h2#references References
          %p Introduction and survey includes
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bertrand+To%C3%ABn"}> Bertrand Toën
                , chapter 4 of
                %em Simplicial presheaves and derived algebraic geometry
                , lecture at
                %a{:href => "http://www.crm.es/HigherCategories/"} Simplicial methods in higher categories
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.crm.cat/HigherCategories/hc1.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li#Toen14
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bertrand+To%C3%ABn"}> Bertrand Toën
                ,
                %em Derived Algebraic Geometry
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1401.1044"}> arXiv:1401.1044
                )
          %p
            See
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+algebras"} model structure on simplicial algebras
            for references on the model structure discussed above.
          %p
            Some of the above material is taken from
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "http://mathoverflow.net/questions/45273/what-facts-in-commutative-algebra-fail-miserably-for-simplicial-commutative-rings"} this MO entry
          %p
            Discussion in the context of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+spectra"} ring spectra
            includes
          %ul
            %li#GoerssHopkins99
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Goerss"}> Paul Goerss
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Hopkins"} Michael Hopkins
              %em Simplicial Structured Ring Spectra
              (1999) (
              %a{:href => "http://citeseerx.ist.psu.edu/viewdoc/summary?doi=10.1.1.34.9216"}> web
              )
